take appropriate measures.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canada, France agree to closer ties in defense, economy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:120801b829a230b0cc962d4004f6e61c4ff63479c76c5be95b0cf5d2fc53a5ef</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T21:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-france-agree-to-closer-ties-in-defense-economy/a-79348843--81fb213bce0f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-france-agree-to-closer-ties-in-defense-economy/a-79348843?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Amid strained relations with the US, French President Emmanuel Macron and Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney announced closer economic and defense ties.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German state elections deal a blow to Chancellor Friedrich Merz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ff88fdad7084b63e39c62d41e5b89841b31d84effcbd175b9a9b7b12708cb6a</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:37Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T21:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-state-elections-deal-a-blow-to-chancellor-friedrich-merz/a-79348585--45dd8fc79779.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-state-elections-deal-a-blow-to-chancellor-friedrich-merz/a-79348585?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Elections in Berlin and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania have dealt the CDU a historic defeat while the AfD saw a massive gain. The pressure on Germany's unpopular chancellor is mounting.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>AfD makes gains in state elections, but has no government options</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ad758eec05f4b86ff2e9f27e05c941b40b259bf76bdce905bf947c528f82fef</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:40Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T19:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afd-makes-gains-in-state-elections-but-has-no-government-options/a-79348308--1a6e760f93a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afd-makes-gains-in-state-elections-but-has-no-government-options/a-79348308?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite making significant gains in both Berlin and Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, the far-right AfD remains without options to form a state government.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Germany faces energy tax losses as EV sales rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4365181c8e184a739439c8c9632c7a564bf0246f6aaf0bd032b535ef6f432b3e</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T14:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422--82b05ee44dbb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-faces-energy-tax-losses-as-ev-sales-rise/a-79320422?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The rapid shift to electric vehicles in Germany is cutting fuel tax revenue for the government. As EV sales surge, policymakers face growing pressure to find new ways to fund roads and transportation infrastructure.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Peter Thiel: Power, Palantir, and the antichrist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5ba43966a741a98ba3826e2929177a9268049960c520112c5b48c7c58604ae7</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T13:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/peter-thiel-power-palantir-and-the-antichrist/a-79313426--884412d8a5b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/peter-thiel-power-palantir-and-the-antichrist/a-79313426?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">He was early to back Facebook, early to back Donald Trump, and is one of the world’s richest people. But from his theories on the antichrist and AI to his distinctive politics, Peter Thiel is hard to pin down.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Russia: Ukrainian drone strike on Moscow kills 2</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f76a30ef9714e1aa71170e74ceb290c55173007373c486b8cb1ddc171087d5d</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T08:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-ukrainian-drone-strike-on-moscow-kills-2/a-79341964--f3da33d772e4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-ukrainian-drone-strike-on-moscow-kills-2/a-79341964?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An oil refinery was hit in one of the largest attacks so far on the Russian capital, as the country holds a parliamentary election. Meanwhile, at least four people were killed in Russian strikes in Ukraine's Kyiv region.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ed Sheeran speaks on Gaza in concert after Macklemore controversy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a49869568744b380cc2ccc6c15503d1c7e41169b948212b16d2609c022c840b7</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T08:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ed-sheeran-speaks-on-gaza-in-concert-after-macklemore-controversy/a-79341971--af13de157344.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ed-sheeran-speaks-on-gaza-in-concert-after-macklemore-controversy/a-79341971?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sheeran called the Hamas-led attack in Israel "horrific" and described the war in Gaza as "catastrophic and unjustifiable" during his first concert since the Macklemore controversy erupted.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>In cosmopolitan Berlin, elections still closed to foreigners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ed74ab8945055e505808507fd07420a1cd0de56855c1cd21e31729e01be3c5e</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T07:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579--2c7a3b66c58f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-cosmopolitan-berlin-elections-still-closed-to-foreigners/a-78744579?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quarter of Berlin residents will have no say in the German capital's city-state election because they lack citizenship. That's the highest proportion of residents excluded from the election yet, and many are unhappy.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>India news: PM Modi says developing nations unfairly blamed for emissions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:591990160d3ecaa054eed6e771d77e335b10e8cfd15c16cfb93e895ca67151f5</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-pm-modi-says-developing-nations-unfairly-blamed-for-emissions/live-79335891--dbd6bc9f1890.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-pm-modi-says-developing-nations-unfairly-blamed-for-emissions/live-79335891?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">PM Narendra Modi has told a climate conference that developed countries emit six times more CO2 than India. Meanwhile, an IIT Bombay professor has been accused of caste abuse. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Doctors offer Oktoberfest flu jabs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8a7bf61bfea25a25e9aa3c1ded3273486861ced79ab3be7e0acd6e90ce0d8c31</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-doctors-offer-oktoberfest-flu-jabs/live-79335548--b4ec07a0d158.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-doctors-offer-oktoberfest-flu-jabs/live-79335548?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Oktoberfest 2026 is underway but it's not just beer on offer in Munich this year; revelers can also get themselves a flu jab before heading to the tents. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Decolonizing perceptions about Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f82c954f968eb5d3570f495e570923497fde4f8978126cdc626ad9fc0f519eca</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/decolonizing-perceptions-about-africa/a-79331178--8deea6e78a06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/decolonizing-perceptions-about-africa/a-79331178?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As a UN resolution alters the standard global map to reflect the continent more accurately, initiatives to decolonize African schools and a campaign to present positive developments are changing the way Africa is seen.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: AfD wins in northeastern state, Left in Berlin</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1df86a4429b236458b7573c9df30485e94bfde83dd650590dd3419a0b6bfa635</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:09:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-voting-underway-in-two-key-state-elections/live-79322092--9f59fbb872c6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-afd-wins-in-northeastern-state-left-in-berlin/live-79322092?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD has come first in the state election in Mecklenburg-Western Pomerania, with Chancellor Merz's CDU failing to enter parliament. Meanwhile the Left Party took first place in Berlin. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany: Is it possible to replace the chancellor?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8baf976eff7145b3e5ad9cb870949704258aa7c68713a5d4aea2b31804202315</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T05:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-is-it-possible-to-replace-the-chancellor/a-79313623--5363f1668974.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-is-it-possible-to-replace-the-chancellor/a-79313623?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chancellor Friedrich Merz's record-low approval ratings have emboldened his opponents. There are three ways to remove a chancellor from office in Germany.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Dutch police disperse violent far-right protest in The Hague</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75f5f86a01743da8312d1765c92be1d3dcf3e8629c1dfa1acfe14c041ef5bcca</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T22:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dutch-police-disperse-violent-far-right-protest-in-the-hague/a-79340495--6f615f4c4297.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dutch-police-disperse-violent-far-right-protest-in-the-hague/a-79340495?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After violence broke out, Dutch riot police dispersed hundreds of far-right protesters in The Hague. Prime Minister Rob Jetten said that the demonstrators had chanted "abhorrent" far-right and antisemitic slogans.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Summer of 2026 broke records in Europe, and caused deaths</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e52c7c73ce7c5d15143f7f1dc15e6b1c69f2004bff0d11c5323c135a6bcae097</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T19:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/summer-of-2026-broke-records-in-europe-and-caused-deaths/a-79339630--5efe97f5474b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/summer-of-2026-broke-records-in-europe-and-caused-deaths/a-79339630?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The summer of 2026 was not only the hottest on record in Europe, it also saw a record number of people die. More than 16,000 are thought to have died because of the heat in Germany alone.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Trump announces new 'AI force' amid mounting pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f1f90859410e0f1b360faceaca1de943a09c4240bb285ff52bde8793e90ceee9</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T17:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-announces-new-ai-force-amid-mounting-pressure/a-79339935--91ffbee2e238.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-announces-new-ai-force-amid-mounting-pressure/a-79339935?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several voices, including from within the AI industry, have been calling for policing the fast-growing technology. Trump has once again called AI warnings "hoaxes" and vowed to "cherish, help" the industry.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German-Russian relations at freezing point</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c191a3b6a156e704764bb945571a3e5292d88140176fcc85abcb4f01efbef32a</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T16:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-russian-relations-at-freezing-point/a-79330741--08a579f047c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-russian-relations-at-freezing-point/a-79330741?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine destroyed the once-close relationship between Moscow and Berlin. Yet the far-right AfD is calling for a normalization of relations.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine steps up measures to protect railways</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e91b668e3f61de742597ceac77f838e8b12082b67688c7dfef5a009743926095</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-steps-up-measures-to-protect-railways/a-79339087--356ca60a409d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-steps-up-measures-to-protect-railways/a-79339087?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russia increases its attacks on Ukraine's rail infrastructure, the Ukrainian government has called for help to replace destroyed locomotives and is making plans to keep passengers safe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>CNN, MS NOW and Politico denied access to White House</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cdd829e6ea53ef533ea0755ee53a306a77c984e6130b6f6ce69e28de21eaba6</id><updated>2026-09-21T05:08:30Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cnn-ms-now-and-politico-denied-access-to-white-house/a-79339055--e53ebc96fb07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cnn-ms-now-and-politico-denied-access-to-white-house/a-79339055?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Three US news outlets said their journalists were blocked from entering the White House grounds, hours after President Donald Trump announced bans on several media outlets.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
